        'FIFO is the default for most businesses because it follows the physical flow of goods, produces an ending inventory close to current replacement cost, and is accepted everywhere. LIFO is a US tax strategy for businesses with large, slow-turning, steadily inflating inventories; it must be elected on IRS Form 970, used in the financial statements too (the conformity rule), and is not permitted under IFRS, which is why foreign-owned or dual-reporting companies avoid it. Weighted average suits fuel, grain, chemicals and any stock where units are interchangeable and purchases frequent.',
